-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC # Creating and Managing Catalogs and Storage
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC This demo provides hands-on experience with Unity Catalog's core storage and governance capabilities. You'll learn to connect external storage systems, implement catalog naming strategies for enterprise environments, and modernize legacy DBFS mount patterns using Unity Catalog constructs.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Unity Catalog provides a unified governance layer for data and AI assets across multiple clouds and platforms. Proper catalog and storage management is essential for implementing data governance at scale while maintaining performance and security requirements.
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 4px solid #ff9800; background: #fff3e0; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0;">
-- MAGIC   <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC     <span style="font-size: 24px;">⚠️</span>
-- MAGIC     <div>
-- MAGIC       This notebook is not supported for execution on Databricks Academy provided workspaces. The material is intended to be a study guide, to be run in your own sandbox environments if you would like. Databricks Academy does not provide an account with a live HMS, administrator level access, or an AWS account, all of which would be required to perform all the activities in these notebooks.<p>
-- MAGIC       <strong>The notebooks flagged as labs in the agenda can be run in a Databricks Academy provided Vocareum workspace and allow you to put the concepts into practice.</strong>
-- MAGIC     </div>
-- MAGIC   </div>
-- MAGIC </div>

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## Learning Objectives
-- MAGIC By the end of this demo, you will be able to:
-- MAGIC - Configure Unity Catalog connections to external cloud storage using storage credentials and external locations
-- MAGIC - Design and implement a catalog naming strategy that supports SDLC and business unit requirements
-- MAGIC - Override managed storage locations to isolate data between catalogs using external locations
-- MAGIC - Apply security best practices for catalog and storage management in enterprise environments

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## A. External Storage Integration with Unity Catalog
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Unity Catalog connects to external cloud storage through two key components: **storage credentials** and **external locations**. Storage credentials contain the authentication information, while external locations define the specific paths and associate them with credentials.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC This approach provides centralized credential management and fine-grained access control over external data sources.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ### A1. Creating Storage Credentials
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 4px solid #ff9800; background: #fff3e0; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0;">
-- MAGIC   <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC     <span style="font-size: 24px;">⚠️</span>
-- MAGIC     <div>
-- MAGIC       Storage credential creation is a privileged operation and can only be performed by an account or metastore admin, or someone with the <code>CREATE STORAGE CREDENTIAL</code> permission on the metastore.
-- MAGIC     </div>
-- MAGIC   </div>
-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Storage credentials securely store authentication information for cloud storage services. They support various authentication methods including service principals, managed identities, and IAM roles.
-- MAGIC <div style="display:flex; justify-content:center;">
