-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Creating storage credentials is done through the **Catalog Explorer** user interface.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC 1. From **Catalog Explorer**, select **Connect &gt; Credentials**.
-- MAGIC 1. In the **Credentials** tab, click **Create credential**.
-- MAGIC 1. With **Storage Credential** selected, select the **Credential Type** (in this case, *AWS IAM Role*).
-- MAGIC 1. Fill in a unique **Credential name**.
-- MAGIC 1. Fill in the **IAM role (ARN)** field.
-- MAGIC 1. Click **Create**.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 4px solid #1976d2; background: #e3f2fd; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0;">
-- MAGIC   <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC     <span style="font-size: 24px;">ℹ️</span>
-- MAGIC     <div>
-- MAGIC       When connecting to new storage locations, you must update the trust relationship in your cloud provider to allow for the Unity Catalog control plane. The Databricks UI provides additional instructions on what needs to be configured.
-- MAGIC     </div>
-- MAGIC   </div>
-- MAGIC </div>

