-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ### A2. Creating External Locations
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 4px solid #ff9800; background: #fff3e0; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0;">
-- MAGIC   <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC     <span style="font-size: 24px;">⚠️</span>
-- MAGIC     <div>
-- MAGIC       External location creation is a privileged operation and can only be performed by an account or metastore admin, or someone with the <code>CREATE EXTERNAL LOCATION</code> permission on the metastore or storage credential.
-- MAGIC     </div>
-- MAGIC   </div>
-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC External locations map storage credentials to specific cloud storage paths. They serve as the foundation for the following important capabilities:
-- MAGIC - **Managed storage overrides:** catalogs (or schemas) can route all data associated with their managed tables or volumes to external cloud storage, allowing for physical isolation at the catalog or schema level
-- MAGIC - **External tables and volumes:** tables and volumes can individually host their data in external cloud storage
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Since external locations can be applied to a path within the storage container, we can associate multiple external locations to a single storage credential.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="display:flex; justify-content:center;">
