-- MAGIC We will implement one set of catalogs using the user interface, and the second set using SQL.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ### B1. Create and Configure Catalogs in the UI
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Let's create and configure catalogs for the finance organization using the UI.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC #### B1.1 Create Catalogs
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC 1. From **Catalog Explorer**, select **Create &gt; Create a catalog**.
-- MAGIC 1. Fill in the first catalog name, *fin_dev*.
-- MAGIC 1. Ensure **Type** is set to *Standard*.
-- MAGIC 1. Click **Create**, and dismiss the **Catalog created** dialog.
-- MAGIC 1. Repeat the process to create a new catalog named *fin_stg*.
-- MAGIC 1. Create a final catalog name *fin_prd*, but recall that this catalog requires isolation. In the **Storage location** section, choose the external location created earlier (two were created; choose the one created for finance purposes). This will route all data to that external cloud location, thereby isolating it as per the requirements.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC #### B1.2 Configure Permissions and Ownerships
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC 1. Still in **Catalog Explorer**, locate and select the `fin_dev` catalog.
-- MAGIC 1. In the **Permissions** tab, click **Grant**.
-- MAGIC 1. Specify the group *finance* for **Principals**.
-- MAGIC 1. To implement "all" permissions, enable the following privileges (see note below):
-- MAGIC    - `USE CATALOG`
-- MAGIC    - `BROWSE`
-- MAGIC    - `CREATE SCHEMA` 
-- MAGIC 1. Click **Confirm**.
-- MAGIC 1. Back in the **Overview** tab, click the pencil next to the **Owner** field. Choose the desired principal (for example, *metastore_admins*) to relinquish ownership to.
-- MAGIC 1. Repeat the process for the `fin_stg` catalog, but reduce privileges to prevent creation of new schemas:
-- MAGIC    - `USE CATALOG`
-- MAGIC    - `BROWSE`
-- MAGIC 1. Adjust ownership of the `fin_stg` catalog.
-- MAGIC 1. Since the requirements specify that `fin_prd` should be restricted, do not grant any privileges; only set ownership.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 4px solid #ff9800; background: #fff3e0; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0;">
